# docker-compose.yml — RETIRED 2026-10-19

The single-service compose spec that used to sit at this path has been
removed: it pinned the retired `loop-depth-v4` image while the service had
moved on, and keeping it meant a deploy from this file would have silently
rolled the image back.

The canonical home for the service definition is now
**dirmacs/infra, `stacks/nimaproxy/`** (per that repo's DEPLOYMENT-MODEL §4:
app source stays here, orchestration lives there). The README in that stack
records the identity rules — in particular, that stack deliberately cannot
recreate or adopt the live container; it is a faithful slice, not the
orchestrator.

This stub exists so `git log -- docker-compose.yml` and old references land
somewhere explanatory instead of on a 404. Safe to delete once nothing
points here anymore.
